haoya main road, approximately 6\u00a0km (3.7\u00a0mi) away from the town of Ampara. The temple has been formally recognised by the Government as an archaeological site in Sri Lanka. It is believed that the temple was built by king Saddha Tissa.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Samanabedda cave temple</b> is an ancient Buddhist temple situated in Uhana, Ampara District, Sri Lanka. The temple lies on the Ampara \u2013 Mahaoya main road, approximately 6\u00a0km (3.7\u00a0mi) away from the town of Ampara. The temple has been formally recognised by the Government as an archaeological site in Sri Lanka. It is believed that the temple was built by king Saddha Tissa.</p>"}